{
 "_why": "Registers that set some visible type under the size floor (runtime/textSafe.tsx TYPE_ERROR_FRAC / TYPE_WARN_FRAC of the frame's short side: ~24 px / ~30 px at 1080). Nothing measured type SIZE before 2026-10-16, and the first sweep found 53 of 194 registers under 24 px and 70 more under 30 px — the library-wide cause of a user's review that the labels were too small to read. In a film, small type on ANY library register is a WARNING (the debt is the library's; a register fed a film's copy can show more than this default-props sweep saw), small type on a film's OWN shot is an ERROR, and the list may only shrink: raise a register's type and re-run the sweep to take it off.",
